Title: Sudan civil war: RSF storms cattle market and prison in 'death trap' city
Date: 2025-07-13
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Mathilde Vu', 'Text': "What we're hearing is stories of horror and terror and weekly shelling, attacks on civilian infrastructure,", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 97}}, {'Speaker': 'Mathilde Vu', 'Text': 'There are local volunteers - they are really struggling, risking their lives every day to try and provide a little bit of food for people who are mostly starving.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 147}}, {'Speaker': 'Siddig Omar', 'Text': 'One of the shells hit a civilian vehicle near my house resulting in the death of five civilians who were inside the car,', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 12, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 101}}, {'Speaker': 'Ms Vu', 'Text': 'People fleeing at night by foot, on donkeys - trying to escape armed men targeting them, maybe raping them,', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 21, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 90}}, {'Speaker': 'Ms Vu', 'Text': "We're getting people arriving into Tawila who are thirsty, who haven't eaten for weeks.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 22, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 74}}, {'Speaker': 'Resident of el-Fasher', 'Text': 'Right now, we are suffering deeply, and everyone around us is facing the same hardship,', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 26, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 77}}, {'Speaker': 'Resident of el-Fasher', 'Text': "There is no bread, no food, and no work to be found. Even if you have money, there's nothing available in the markets to buy.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 27, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 116}}, {'Speaker': 'Resident of el-Fasher', 'Text': "When someone gets sick, we can't find any medicine or treatment.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 28, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 61}}, {'Speaker': 'Resident of el-Fasher', 'Text': 'There are no medicines in hospitals. The situation here is truly terrible.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 29, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 69}}, {'Speaker': 'Another man', 'Text': 'We are in a very critical situation,', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 31, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 34}}, {'Speaker': 'Another man', 'Text': 'Even ombaz is no longer available, as the peanut factories have stopped working.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 32, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 72}}, {'Speaker': 'Another man', 'Text': 'We are calling out for help - please, we urgently need assistance,', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 33, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 63}}, {'Speaker': 'Ms Vu', 'Text': 'The funding is completely decreasing and the consequence is that you can see it on the ground,', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 35, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 89}}, {'Speaker': 'Ms Vu', 'Text': 'People [in el-Fasher] just rely on the solidarity of others.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 36, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 56}}, {'Speaker': 'Ms Vu', 'Text': 'If they have a little bit of food, they will be sharing it among themselves.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 37, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 77}}], 'Description': [{'Description': 'The Sudanese paramilitary group Rapid Support Forces (RSF) stormed the besieged city of el-Fasher on Friday in a battle that raged for seven hours, witnesses told the BBC.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 1, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 141}}, {'Description': 'RSF fighters managed to capture a cattle market, a prison and a military base while broadcasting videos of themselves walking around empty stockyards.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 2, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 153}}, {'Description': 'On Saturday morning, the army retaliated and succeeded in pushing the RSF back beyond el-Fasher\'s limits. But Mathilde Vu, from the Norwegian Refugee Council (NRC), described the city as a "death trap".', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 190}}, {'Description': 'Siddig Omar, a 65-year-old resident of el-Fasher, told the BBC the RSF entered the city on Friday from the south and south-west.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 110}}, {'Description': "But this time, during a battle that raged for seven hours, they managed to take control of the city's livestock market, which has been closed for business for several months.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 8, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 156}}, {'Description': "From here, they broadcast videos of their fighters walking around empty stockyards. They also briefly held Shalla prison and the headquarters of the military's Central Reserve Forces.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 9, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 162}}, {'Description': 'On Saturday morning, the army retaliated and succeeded in pushing the RSF back beyond the city limits, saying it had inflicted "heavy losses" on the paramilitary group.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 10, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 149}}, {'Description': 'But Mr Omar said RSF shelling - using drones - continued throughout Saturday.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 11, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 72}}, {'Description': 'Nearly 379,000 people have now fled to Tawila, where they are facing an outbreak of cholera and expected heavy rain is likely to destroy makeshift shelters.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 23, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 137}}, {'Description': "This week, residents of el-Fasher told the BBC Arabic's emergency radio programme more about their dire situation.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 24, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 93}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': "A screengrab of two RSF fighters in el-Fasher's cattle market - one with a belt of ammunition around his neck holds up a victory sign"}]}
